{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"shaggy-crass-bull","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Problem\n\nThree defensive `except`/`isinstance` arms that decide whether an LLM-tier failure ABORTS or\nDEGRADES have **no test that reaches them**. Found by the Step-7 parity sweep while fixing bug\n`wolflike-chevroned-haddock` (`43d4-b8f5-4bb2-417b`).\n\nDemonstrated by mutation: reverting each arm to its pre-fix form leaves the **entire** unit\nsuite green.\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/workflow/gate_dispatch.py` mid-run plan-review arm (~:189) and mid-run\n  code-review arm (~:522). These `try` blocks have no broad `except`, so an escaping error\n  loses the `gate_error_v1` sidecar and the degraded-verdict contract. A probe driving\n  `produce_plan_review_verdict` with a runner whose `preflight` passes and whose `run` raises\n  could not reach either arm — the workflow executor absorbs the failure into the\n  finders-failed tail first — and that is true for the **pre-existing** `LLMUnavailableError`\n  too, so this is not a gap introduced by 43d4. It is unclear from outside whether these arms\n  are reachable at all; if they are not, they are dead code and should be removed rather than\n  maintained.\n- `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/container_stage.py` warm-call abort (~:209). `container_stage`\n  has **zero** referencing tests, so the whole module's abort-vs-degrade decision is unpinned.\n\n## Why it matters\n\nThese arms encode cost and fail-closed rulings (abort rather than fan out N-1 doomed calls;\nnever degrade a blind run into a clean result). An unpinned ruling silently stops holding the\nnext time the exception vocabulary moves — which is exactly what bug 43d4 was.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A test reaches `gate_dispatch`'s mid-run plan-review arm and asserts the degraded verdict\n      plus the emitted `gate_error_v1` sidecar — or, if the arm is proven unreachable, it is\n      removed and that removal is recorded with the evidence.\n- [ ] The same for the mid-run code-review arm.\n- [ ] A test drives `container_stage`'s warm-call path and asserts the abort, so reverting the\n      `isinstance` arm turns it RED.\n- [ ] Each new test is shown to FAIL when its arm is reverted (a recorded mutation check), not\n      merely to pass.","id":"c72a-48be-054d-4005","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Untested mid-run/warm-call fail-closed arms in gate_dispatch and container_stage"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787320693786502001,"uuid":"282b9e56-c137-4b64-80b8-f0b2369f7a18"}